The theorems quantify over:
- every d : ℕ;
- L : ℝ with hL : 0 < L;
- g : E d → ℝ, where E d = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) (Lifetime.lean line 76), with:
  - IsSmooth d g: ∀ n : ℕ, ContDiff ℝ n g (Lifetime.lean lines 136-137);
  - IsLPeriodic d L g: g (x + latticeVec d L n) = g x for all x and all n : Fin d → ℤ (lines 127-128);
  - IsMorseDistinct d L g (lines 311-314): every critical point has a Hessian inertia index, and critical values at positive torus distance are distinct;
- M : E d with ¬ superlevelBar_isEssential g M, where SuperlevelBar.lean lines 46-48 define essential as ∀ y, g y ≤ g M. M need not be a critical point or a local maximum;
- the explicit premise hclosedLPC : LocallyPathConnectedSpace {q : torus_quotient d L hL // superlevelBar_deathHeight g M ≤ descendedHeight d L hL g hperiodic q}.
Definitions behind the statements:
- descendedHeight is torus_descend of g (lines 26-28).
- superlevelBar_deathHeight is the sSup of the strict-clearance set, with default 0 when that set is empty (SuperlevelBar.lean lines 60-64). The strict-clearance set holds the heights h for which some path runs from M to a strictly higher y with g > h along it (lines 53-55).
- In the conclusions, IsCriticalPoint d g y means fderiv ℝ g y = 0 (Lifetime.lean lines 197-198).
- quotientCriticalSet d L hL g is the torus_proj image of {x | IsCriticalPoint d g x} (MorseFiniteCritical.lean lines 150-152).
The source states that only the nondegeneracy conjunct of IsMorseDistinct is used, through quotientCriticalSet_finite (AUTHOR_NOTES.md lines 47-51). MorseFiniteCritical.lean line 221 passes hmorse.1.

statements.text:
The same join governs joint options. A dynamic memory does not have to refine all required partitions simultaneously; it only has to refine the right suffix at the right time, subject to causal update feasibility.

This yields the distinction between:

- static memory, which must refine the partition join;
- dynamic memory, whose required capacity is bounded below by the largest stage partition but is not always causally attainable;
- nonmonotone information trajectories, which are not filtrations because useful forgetting can coarsen information.
